ass", "lead_before": 14.21, "lead_after": 14.19, "points_lost": -0.02, "best": "pass"}, {"turn": 63, "color": "B", "move": "pass", "lead_before": 14.19, "lead_after": 14.0, "points_lost": 0.19, "best": "G9"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "A Lead Handed Back, Then Passed Back and Forth", "summary": "The 14k won as Black by 14 points after both sides spent the middle game giving away big leads. Opus 5.5 was ahead after Black's C3 at move 11 (lead -8.6), but D6 at move 22 gave it back, and H5 at move 30 swung the game to Black +70.3. The 14k then gave much of that back in a run of 56 to 60-point swings, but kept a final lead of +14.0.", "moments": [{"turn": 11, "text": "Black's C3 lost 8.8 points, the lead moving from +0.2 to -8.6, and the engine preferred E7. It was the 14k's first big slip, and it left Opus 5.5 ahead on the left side, with White stones at D3 and D2 against Black's C3 and C2."}, {"turn": 22, "text": "With the lead at -9.0, Opus 5.5 played D6 and lost 9.8 points, moving it to +0.8. The engine's choice was F7. This threw away the advantage built after move 11 and made it a game again."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "E6 cost 12.1 points (+2.4 to +14.5), and the engine wanted E1. This began a stretch in which Opus 5.5 lost 12.1, 21.3 and then 65.1 points on its next three moves."}, {"turn": 30, "text": "The decisive blunder: H5 lost 65.1 points, taking the lead from +5.2 to +70.3. The engine's choice was D1. Black's wall on G7, H7, G6 and the G3 to H3 stones was already strong, and this move made it overwhelming."}, {"turn": 47, "text": "At +72.5, Black played F1 and lost 59.7 points, dropping to +12.8. The engine preferred J2. Opus 5.5 answered with G2 at move 48, which lost 61.3 points and sent the lead back to +74.0."}, {"turn": 53, "text": "The swinging continued. White's B3 at move 52 lost 58.5 points, and Black's B2 right after lost 58.4, pulling the lead down to +15.5. Opus 5.5's J2 at move 54 then lost nothing (-0.9), but by then the game was settled at about B+14."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The only program run was libs.py, which parses a board pasted on stdin and flood-fills each group to print its stones and liberties; the other commands just tail/cat games.md and append a game log entry. None of it chooses, ranks or looks ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}